AB  - The proceedings contain 27 papers. The topics discussed include: a dynamic and autonomous channel selection strategy for interference avoidance in 802.11; on the feasibility of collision detection in full-duplex 802.11 radio; TraceMixer: privacy-preserving crowd-sensing sans trusted third party; on the sensitivity of geo-based content sharing to location errors; the more you speak, the less you hear: on dynamic announcement intervals in wireless on-demand networks; promotion of cooperation in public goods game by socialized speed-restricted movement; offloading on the edge: performance and cost analysis of local data storage and offloading in HetNets; active energy management for harvesting enabled wireless sensor network; energy-efficient analog sensing for large scale, high-density persistent wireless monitoring; on the application of LoRa LPWAN technology in sailing monitoring system; an alternative congestion control using an enhanced contention based forwarding for vehicular networks; efficient mmwave wireless backhauling for dense small-cell deployments; dynamic RPL for multi-hop routing in IoT applications; and an SMDP approach to optimal PHY configuration in wireless networks.
