AB  - Although LoRaWAN standard has recently issued relay specification used for multi-hop communication, its application has not been prevalent. This paper proposes multi-hop capability, coupled with multi-copy, spatially confined-broadcast message routing for Lora-based network. To reduce the impact of medium access contention, local slotted Aloha is utilized, and enhance it with sender-aware forwarding scheme. We also extend its capability to facilitate handshaking communication. Developing this capability aims at larger network coverage, complex network topology, and provides reliable message delivery when poor links are expected within the network. We developed multi-hop-capable LoRa devices prototype and deploy them in a meshtopology network. Packet delivery rate and latency are evaluated. The result shows that our developed multi-hop capability, coupled with spatially-confined broadcast routing protocol for message delivery and handshaking, can achieve above 95 percent packet delivery rate with acceptable latency in mesh network and effectively mitigate the impact of poor link within the network  © 2025 IEEE.
