AD  - Bangladesh University of Business and Technology, Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Dhaka, Bangladesh
AB  - Bangladesh's water utilities face severe challenges from outdated analog metering, including high water losses, revenue shortfalls, and inequitable distribution. This paper presents a smart water-metering system that leverages Internet of Things (IoT) sensors and artificial intelligence to modernize water-distribution management. The proposed solution enables real-time monitoring of water usage and quality via IoT-enabled flow and water-quality sensors, delivering instantaneous data to utilities and consumers. A machine learning anomaly detection module (Isolation Forest) identifies leaks, pipe bursts, and unauthorized consumption by flagging outlier usage patterns. To ensure reliable communication under diverse infrastructural conditions, the system supports multi-mode data transmission Wi-Fi, GSM cellular, LoRa long-range radio, Bluetooth mesh relay, and Ethernet. A smart billing platform with web and mobile interfaces automates meter reading, billing, and payment through digital wallets, improving transparency and convenience. The hardware is engineered for uninterrupted operation during loadshedding and power outages using a battery backup design. We evaluate monitoring accuracy, anomaly detection performance, and communication reliability; results demonstrate effective realtime usage tracking, timely leak/theft detection, and improved billing efficiency. © 2025 IEEE.
