AD  - Laboratory of Electronics, Antenna and Telecommunication (LEAT), Universite Cote D’Azur, France
AD  - Danang International Institute of Technology, University of Danang, Viet Nam
AB  - This chapter introduces an innovative Internet of Things (IoT) system designed for efficient energy management in smart mesh networks, leveraging hybrid renewable energy sources for environmental monitoring. The proposed system, an energy-efficient solution for WSNs using LoRa Mesh technology integrated with the Ad-hoc On-Demand Distance Vector (AODV) routing algorithm, addresses the challenges of energy consumption and connectivity in remote areas with unstable power supplies and harsh conditions. Using solar power supplemented by battery backup, the system ensures reliable data transmission while minimizing energy consumption during severe weather, with devices capable of functioning for up to a month solely on battery backup. Field experiments in Vietnam highlight its effectiveness, showcasing improved energy efficiency and extended operational range, and demonstrate that the proposed system achieves a packet delivery success rate (DSR) of 95%–99%, reduces packet loss to 1%–5%. The solution not only enhances reliability in remote areas without 3G/4G coverage but also supports sustainable IoT applications in hybrid renewable energy systems. Copyright © The Institution of Engineering and Technology and its licensors 2026 First published 2025.
