AB  - Natural disasters often disrupt communication infrastructure, limiting Internet access for emergency response. This paper presents an experimentally validated heterogeneous UAV swarm network integrating WiFi access, multi-hop relaying, LTE backhaul, and LoRa coordination. Propagation models are validated using real RSSI measurements and mean absolute error analysis. End-to-end performance is evaluated through real flight experiments under line-of-sight (LoS) and obstructed conditions, considering delivery success probability and latency. Results identify an RSSI operating region near $-65 \mathbf{~ d B m}$ associated with stable service, revealing the coupling between link margin and QoS in multi-hop UAV networks. These findings provide practical guidelines for relay spacing and rapid deployment of UAV-based communication systems in post-disaster scenarios. © 2026 IEEE.
