AB  - This paper demonstrates a practical forest fire detection system leveraging LoRa technology, integrating a fire sensor with an energy-efficient cluster head. By exploiting the system’s low-power features and utilizing LoRaWAN for extended communication range, the solution enables real-time monitoring in remote regions through multi-hop routing, offering a scalable and energy-efficient approach. The topology ensures efficient data transmission between fire sensors and the central monitoring station, enabling swift reactions to potential forest fires. The optimized low-power modes contribute to prolonged battery life, crucial for sustained operation in challenging environments. This implementation not only addresses deployment challenges but also serves as a valuable reference for practitioners working on similar systems in expansive landscapes, contributing to the ongoing advancements in wildfire detection technology. © 2026 Scrivener Publishing LLC.
