AD  - Kongu Engineering College, Department of EEE, Tamil Nadu, India
AB  - The natural disasters such as floods, earthquakes, and cyclones have the potential of devastating the normal communication systems; hence information flow is very crucial in rescue and relief operations. The project involves a LoRabased mesh network, which will be used to create a natural disaster communication system with a long-range and lowpower communication that will not rely on infrastructures to send data. The suggested system would be made of LoRaequipped nodes installed throughout the impacted area and create a self-organizing multi-hop mesh network. The nodes can detect and transmit important information including environmental information, location information and emergency alerts and pass information of the neighbouring nodes to ensure network connectivity, even when a node or a link fails to operate. A gateway node collects the transmitted data and sends the data to a local server where it is processed, stored, and visualized. It includes a graphical user interface (GUI) through which you can monitor the health of the network, the state of nodes, signal strength, and disasters and receive alerts in real-time. The system has been designed keeping in mind robustness, scalability, and power consumption; hence, the system is ideal in places where rapid deployment is necessary, or remote locations where disasters are likely to plague. The offered LoRa-based mesh network offers an option to have a decentralized data structure that guarantees situational data backup and emergency response in case of natural disasters. The performance of the proposed system is evaluated through the experimental setup consists of three nodes. © 2026 IEEE.
