AB  - In order to ensure that wireless node devices access enough terminal sensors in the sensing layer and establish a wireless terminal network based on LoRa to provide continuous sensing data for the upper layer, a hardware architecture scheme of high-performance processor + cortex-M4 dual processor is proposed, accurate slot allocation and scheduling algorithm is designed to realize terminal access technology, and unordered tree data structure is used to construct wireless network routing algorithm to realize ad hoc network technology. The wireless node equipment can support 4000 sensor terminals to access, has accurate DRX scheduling, multi-hop can reach more than 10 levels, and can meet various application scenarios of power transmission and transformation. By using networking technology, wireless node equipment can realize the networking of terminal devices through walls and send sensing data, which brings convenience to site construction, reduces the maintenance cost after system operation, and promotes the more intelligent and networked development of the wireless sensing system. © 2023 IEEE.
