UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105044694300?origin=resultslist
AD  - Dsce, Dept. of Eee, Bengaluru, India
AB  - Urban traffic is continuously growing in volume, and new problems arise, including congestion, delays, emergencies, and poor real-time coordination of vehicles. Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) utilize Vehicle-to-Vehicle (V2V) communications to overcome these problems by using cooperative awareness and safety technologies. This paper describes a LoRa-based V2V framework that includes an ESP32-CAM and is connected to the cloud, which detects an emergency by employing an inertial sensor, sends alerts to nearby vehicles and ambulances with multi-hop LoRa relays, detects congestion by aggregating vehicle speed data, and monitors the length of the stop against a stop length threshold. Each vehicle uploads traffic data to the cloud, enabling pilot studies on the framework. The contribution to original knowledge is the engineering of crash alerts, congestion management, and cloud analytics into a single platform. The framework enhances road safety, reduces the emergency response time and accelerates proactivity in traffic management.  © 2025 IEEE.
