AB  - Most if the tracking systems that are available in market are limited by their use of cellular connectivity, short-range communication and high-power consumption. This paper proposes a GPS tracking and alert system based on LoRa technology, designed for individuals working in or exploring remote areas with no connectivity. It enables low-power, long-range communication independent of cellular networks. The prototype implements two-way LoRa communication through the REYAX RYLR998 module and fetches real time GPS coordinates through the NEO-M8N sensor, which is all controlled by ESP32 microcontroller. It works on a mesh-based structure, where each device can act as a relay node. The proposed model is as an energy-efficient, long-range alternative that can function in environments with no cellular networks.  © 2025 IEEE.
