AB  - This paper presents a wearable IoT-based rescue system designed to enhance mountain emergency response in offgrid environments. The proposed platform integrates low-power LoRa mesh communication, ESP32-based physiological monitoring, and a GIS-assisted command center dashboard. By combining long-range mesh connectivity with real-time health sensing, the system enables distress alerts and situational awareness even when cellular networks fail. Field experiments demonstrated communication ranges up to 6 km in open terrain and reliable message relays in mountainous regions. The integration of physiological monitoring provides vital information for rescue coordination and personnel safety. This study aims to contribute to Taiwan's disaster-resilience framework by introducing a scalable, decentralized communication solution for mountain rescue operations.  © 2026 IEEE.
