AB  - This article presents the development of a meteorological data collection and transmission system utilizing wireless sensor networks (WSNs) based on LoRa technology. The study examines approaches to message routing in sensor networks, including centralized and decentralized algorithms, as well as methods for enhancing network fault tolerance and optimizing energy consumption. A self-organizing network algorithm, based on energy metrics such as device battery level, is proposed to optimize routing paths. The work also investigates a mechanism for configuring radio module parameters to reduce the energy costs associated with data transmission. Simulation results demonstrate a significant reduction in energy consumption, confirming the proposed system's effectiveness for real-world applications. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
