AB  - The proceedings contain 23 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Ad-Hoc Networks and Wireless. The topics include: Energy Saving in TSCH Networks by Means of Proactive Reduction of Idle Listening; towards Long-Lasting Nanoscale Wireless Communications in the Terahertz Band for Biomedical Applications; New CAP Reduction Mechanisms for IEEE 802.15.4 DSME to Support Fluctuating Traffic in IoT Systems; testing and Evaluating a Security-Aware Pub and Sub Protocol in a Fog-Driven IoT Environment; XSS Attack Detection Model Based on Semi-supervised Learning Algorithm with Weighted Neighbor Purity; A Cross-Layer Intrusion Detection System for RPL-Based Internet of Things; secure Energy Constrained LoRa Mesh Network; CROSS City: Wi-Fi Location Proofs for Smart Tourism; total Transmission Time Minimization Through Relay Selection for Full-Duplex Wireless Powered Cooperative Communication Networks; Towards Named AI Networking: Unveiling the Potential of NDN for Edge AI; energy Aware Epidemic Strategies for Mobile Opportunistic Networks; Integrating an MQTT Proxy in a LoRa-Based Messaging System for Generic Sensor Data Collection; A Fault Tolerant LoRa/LoRaWAN Relay Protocol Using LoRaWAN Class A Devices; IETF Reliable and Available Wireless (RAW): Use Cases and Problem Statement; fast and Cost-Efficient Virtualized Network Function Placement Algorithm in Wireless Multi-hop Networks; Evaluation of DTN Routing Algorithms in Scheduled Public Transport Networks; geocaching-Inspired Navigation for Micro Aerial Vehicles with Fallible Place Recognition; a Dual-Stack Communication System for the Internet of Drones; consensus-Based Algorithms for Controlling Swarms of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles; STOP: A Location Spoofing Resistant Vehicle Inspection System; a Simulation Framework for QoE-Aware Real-Time Video Streaming in Multipath Scenarios.
